      "dom_id": "step-q60243",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nA jar contains $7$ pounds of pinto beans and $9$ pounds of black beans, so there are $\\boxed{}$ pounds of pinto beans for each pound of black beans.",
      "worked_solution": "The ratio of the number of pounds of pinto beans to the number of pounds of black beans is  $7:9.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{9}\n$$\n\nThis means that there are $\\frac{7}{9}$ pounds of pinto beans for each pound of black beans.",
