      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nJason bought $2$ kilograms of almonds and $3$ kilograms of peanuts, so there are $\\boxed{}$ kilograms of almonds for each kilogram of peanuts.",
      "worked_solution": "The ratio of the amount of almonds to the amount of peanuts is  $2:3.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nThis means that Jason has $\\frac{2}{3}$ kilograms of almonds for each kilogram of peanuts.",
