      "problem": "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nAnna requires $\\frac{1}{10}$ ounce of cocoa powder for every ounce of sugar to make a chocolate cake. Therefore, the cake has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ ounce of cocoa powder to $\\boxed{}$ ounces of sugar.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{1}{10}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n1:10\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cake has a ratio of $1$ ounce of cocoa powder to $10$ ounces of sugar.",
