      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nJoanna cooks rice for lunch. According to the recipe, the ratio of cups of rice to cups of water is $2:4,$ so $\\boxed{}$ cups of rice are needed for each cup of water.",
      "worked_solution": "We can rewrite the ratio $2:4$ as the following fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac{2÷2}{4÷2}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\frac{1}{2}$ cups of rice are needed for each cup of water.",
